### =========================================================
### Compatibility feature + TMDB search/import + top-rated
### Run these IN ORDER, top to bottom as each later request
### depends on data captured from an earlier one via
### client.global.set(...)
###
### If you re-run this file a second time, step 1/2/12 will
### fail with DuplicateUsernameException/DuplicateEmailException
### since the usernames/emails are hardcoded so just tweak them
### (e.g. alice_test2) and rerun from the top.
### =========================================================

### 1. Register user A
POST http://localhost:8080/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice_test1",
  "email": "alice_test1@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

> {%
client.global.set("tokenA", response.body.token);
client.global.set("userIdA", response.body.user.id);
%}


### 2. Register user B
POST http://localhost:8080/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "bob_tes1t",
  "email": "bob_test1@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

> {%
client.global.set("tokenB", response.body.token);
client.global.set("userIdB", response.body.user.id);
%}


### 3. A follows B
POST http://localhost:8080/users/following
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

{
  "followeeId": {{userIdB}}
}


### 4. B follows A back (now mutual)
POST http://localhost:8080/users/following
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenB}}

{
  "followeeId": {{userIdA}}
}


### 5. Search TMDB for a movie (no auth needed, GET routes are public)
### Expect: 200 + a JSON array of TMDB results, including the real "Inception" (tmdbId 27205)
GET http://localhost:8080/movies/search?title=inception


### 6. Import that movie by tmdbId
### Expect: 201 + the saved Movie, with a real internal "id"
POST http://localhost:8080/movies/import
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

{
  "tmdbId": 27205
}

> {%
client.global.set("movieId", response.body.id);
%}


### 7. A reviews the movie
### Expect: 201 + the saved Review
POST http://localhost:8080/movies/{{movieId}}/reviews
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

{
  "rating": 9
}


### 8. B reviews the same movie
### Expect: 201 + the saved Review
POST http://localhost:8080/movies/{{movieId}}/reviews
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenB}}

{
  "rating": 7
}


### 9. Check top-rated movies
### Expect: 200 + this movie included, with averageRating = 8.0 (average of 9 and 7)
GET http://localhost:8080/movies/top-rated


### 10. Check compatibility, A's perspective
### Expect: 200 + a real compatibilityScore (not null) and 1 entry in sharedMovies
### (|9-7|=2 difference -> 100 - (2/9*100) ≈ 77.8% compatible)
GET http://localhost:8080/users/compatibility/{{userIdB}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}


### 11. Check compatibility, B's perspective (should mirror #10, myRating/theirRating swapped)
GET http://localhost:8080/users/compatibility/{{userIdA}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenB}}


### 12. Register user C — nobody follows them, used to test rejection below
POST http://localhost:8080/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "charlie_test1",
  "email": "charlie_test1@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

> {%
client.global.set("userIdC", response.body.user.id);
%}


### 13. Compatibility check against C, who A doesn't follow
### Expect: 403 NotMutualFollowException
GET http://localhost:8080/users/compatibility/{{userIdC}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}


### 14. Compatibility check with no token at all
### Expect: 401 Unauthorized (proves the "GET but still needs auth" before-handler carve-out works)
GET http://localhost:8080/users/compatibility/{{userIdB}}


### 15. Sanity check: zero shared movies case
### Register user D, mutually follow with A, but review nothing —
### Expect: 200 + compatibilityScore: null, sharedMovies: []
POST http://localhost:8080/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "dana_test1",
  "email": "dana_test1@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

> {%
client.global.set("tokenD", response.body.token);
client.global.set("userIdD", response.body.user.id);
%}

### 15b. A follows D
POST http://localhost:8080/users/following
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

{
  "followeeId": {{userIdD}}
}

### 15c. D follows A back
POST http://localhost:8080/users/following
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenD}}

{
  "followeeId": {{userIdA}}
}

### 15d. Compatibility between A and D — no shared reviews yet
### Expect: 200 + compatibilityScore: null, sharedMovies: []
GET http://localhost:8080/users/compatibility/{{userIdD}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}
